<title>UK: Sears maintains total dividend for year.</title>
<headline>Sears maintains total dividend for year.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to January 31, 1997</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		 3.3		   vs  7.1 loss</p>
<p> Shr adjusted		4.3		   vs  6.0</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	  2.90		  vs  n/a</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence)  3.95		  vs  3.95</p>
<p> Pretax pre-excepts	88.9		  vs  70.8</p>
<p> Turnover		    1.95 billion	vs  2.34</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts had forecast pre-tax profits in a range between 75 and 80 million stg. The profits figure above was before tax and exceptional charges but includes a 7.9 million stg pension credit. Profit before tax was 68.1 million stg.</p>
<p>Sears said overall like-for-like sales were up 5.3 percent in the first 11 weeks of the current year.</p>
<p>Full company name - Sears Plc</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 4365</p>
</text>
